# Pairs with OwnerMonotonic. The retroactive sweep does not replay an undecided
# prepare that predates the split window, so once the map moves k2 to the
# destination the destination has neither the bucket nor the row, and a commit
# a reader already saw on the source reverts.
MODULE: OwnerMonotonicSweepSkipsReplay
TARGET: OwnerMonotonic
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the retroactive sweep drops an undecided prepare, so a visible commit reverts when the map moves
PERTURBS: SplitSweep

--- FIND
               ELSE /\ pend' = [x \in Copies |-> [s \in Shards |-> [k \in Keys |->
                                   IF <<x, s>> \in dests /\ k = k2 THEN b ELSE pend[x][s][k]]]]
                    /\ UNCHANGED <<row, term>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an undecided bucket is not replayed to the destination.
               ELSE UNCHANGED <<row, pend, term>>
--- END